course: dictionary
lesson: 1446
title: What does cartoon mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cartoon has three main meanings. It can be a film or TV show made from drawings or computer pictures that move, usually funny. It can be a funny drawing in a newspaper or magazine, often about the news. It can also be a short story told in drawn pictures, like a comic strip.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. «In the cartoon «Ice Age» a mammoth, a sabre-toothed cat and a ground sloth travel together» tells you that Ice Age is a film, because animals travel together in it and they never talked. «Popeye is a cartoon that exaggerates on purpose» also means a film, because exaggerates means makes things bigger than they really are.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If «the cartoon idea that mice love cheese» still makes sense with «the film idea» or «the wrong idea», you have found the right meaning.
fact: A cartoon can be a moving film or TV show, a funny drawing in a newspaper, or a short story in pictures.
fact: Cartoons often exaggerate on purpose, so Popeye's muscles can appear too quickly; real muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest.
fact: Cartoon tricks, such as falling off a cliff and being fine, are not real, so never copy them.
fact: Cartoons can give wrong ideas about real animals: «the cartoon idea that mice love cheese above everything is not true», because house mice mainly eat seeds, grain and crumbs.
fact: A koala is not a bear, and a real Tasmanian devil does not spin like Taz, though it screeches and eats bones and fur.
exercise: In the sentence «In the cartoon «Ice Age» a mammoth, a sabre-toothed cat and a ground sloth travel together», what kind of thing is Ice Age? | A book with no pictures | *A film made from moving drawings or computer pictures | A real farm full of animals | A newspaper picture about the news
exercise: The sentence «the cartoon idea that mice love cheese above everything is not true» shows that a cartoon can do what? | *Give a wrong idea about real animals | Show mice really do love cheese more than anything | Make cheese bad for mice | Show that mice live only in fields
exercise: Ella says a cartoon strip is a silly phrase. What does cartoon strip mean? | A long train of cars | A strip of cloth used in art | A film with no sound | *A short story told in drawn pictures
test: «Taz of Looney Tunes spins like a tornado and eats everything.» Which fact is true about a real Tasmanian devil? | It is a bear that lives in trees | It lives in houses and eats cheese | *It does not spin, though it screeches and eats bones and fur | It spins like a tornado
test: A funny drawing in a newspaper, about the news, is an example of what? | A map of the town | A computer game | *A cartoon, meaning a funny drawing | A moving film
exam: «Popeye is a cartoon that exaggerates on purpose.» What does exaggerates mean here? | *Makes things bigger or stronger than they really are | Draws everything in black and white | Tells the true story exactly | Makes things look smaller than they are
